From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Jerphanion <git@jjerphan.xyz>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 11:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Skip wasm longdouble quantile interpolation

Emscripten long double is IEEE binary128. np.quantile(..., 0.4) with
longdouble still sees 0.4 as a binary64 value (or strtold binary64),
so inverted_cdf / averaged_inverted_cdf pick the wrong order statistic
(35 instead of 20 / 27.5). Skip those cases on wasm.

Signed-off-by: Julien Jerphanion <git@jjerphan.xyz>
---
 numpy/lib/tests/test_function_base.py | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/numpy/lib/tests/test_function_base.py b/numpy/lib/tests/test_function_base.py
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/numpy/lib/tests/test_function_base.py
+++ b/numpy/lib/tests/test_function_base.py
@@ -3433,6 +3433,11 @@ class TestPercentile:
                                   expected_dtype):
         expected_dtype = np.dtype(expected_dtype)
 
+        if IS_WASM and input_dtype is np.longdouble:
+            pytest.skip(
+                "wasm IEEE-quad longdouble makes quantile 0.4 pick the wrong order statistic"
+            )
+
         arr = np.asarray([15.0, 20.0, 35.0, 40.0, 50.0], dtype=input_dtype)
         weights = np.ones_like(arr) if weighted else None
         if input_dtype is np.longdouble:
